doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22030395
identifiers:
  # A version DOI cannot live inside the tree that produces it — it is minted when the
  # release is published. v1.1-paper hardcoded the *previous* number and called itself
  # "SDKB v1.0"; that is the defect this release closes. The concept DOI is stable and
  # lists every version, so it is the only DOI this file states.
  - type: url
    value: "https://github.com/arkwith7/sdkb-dataset/tree/v1.1.1-paper"
    description: "Tagged tree of this release — its version DOI is listed on the concept record."
version: "1.1.1"
date-released: "2026-08-21"
license: CDLA-Permissive-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/arkwith7/sdkb-dataset"
abstract: >-
  SDKB is a provenance-grounded curation knowledge base that serves as the
  semiconductor-domain data trunk for the SKKU Quantitative Technology
  Management Lab's research agenda — patent/market/industry-driven tech
  foresight, emerging-technology opportunity discovery, SME innovation and
  expert matching, and interactive technology/business data visualization.
  It integrates manufacturing process, equipment, material, FMEA, and
  multi-jurisdiction regulatory layers with patent classification, RBV,
  commercialization, and foresight modules. The Semiconductor Industry
  Rejected Patents (SIRP) dataset adds 773 examiner-grounded prior-art
  labels supporting SDKB-Match (the SDKB Matching Layer for semiconductor
  SME ↔ expert and patent ↔ prior-art matching), the first concrete
  implementation of the lab's compliance-aware semantic collaboration vision.
keywords:
  - semiconductor
  - ontology
  - knowledge-graph
  - patent-analytics
  - prior-art-retrieval
  - expert-matching
  - technology-management
  - FMEA
  - foresight
  - export-control
references:
